  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 355 AM EDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nStarting off the long term outlook on Friday, the upper level wave \nbreak pattern will continue to bring scattered to widespread showers \nand thunderstorms to much of north and central GA. PWATs in excess \nof 2 inches will mean heavy soaking rains may continue from previous \ndays. The overall risk for severe weather through the long term \nremains fairly low. Thunderstorms on Friday are likely to develop in \nareas which have already been worked over with limited organization.\n\nMoving into the weekend, upper level flow shifts eastward \nbringing broad ridging back overhead. High temperatures will return \nto the 90s with dewpoints in the 70s. Just another blast of the \nsummer sauna. Thunderstorms potential drops through the weekend, \nthough isolated to scattered diurnally driven thunderstorms remain \npossible. PWATs falling below 2 inches will also reduce the risk for \nflash flooding.",
